# reading_translation = The second book gives the grammar of the Kawi language, taken from the portion of the Kawi poem Brata-Yuddha printed in Raffles' History of Java, everywhere in comparison with the grammar of the remaining languages of the Malay stock, under which name the inhabitants of all the islands of the great southern ocean are comprehended together with the population of Malacca, whose languages, together with that called Malay in the narrower sense, on Malacca, belong to one and the same stock.
