# sent_id = orat18.1.21
# text = Scheiden wir dasjenige aus, was Leibniz, eben weil er nicht genau sonderte, aus diesem Gebiete in seinen Begriff der Gelehrsamkeit hineinzuziehen scheint, so befafst er unter dieser nach seinen eigenen Worten alles, was wir von den Menschen lernen, im Gegensatze gegen das, was aus dem Geiste erfunden wird; sie unterscheidet sich ihm von der Philosophie, wie das was thatsächlich ist (quod est facti), von dem, was Sache der reinen Erkenntniſs oder des Rechtes ist (quod est rationis sive iuris).
# reading_translation = If we set aside whatever Leibniz, precisely because he did not distinguish carefully, seems to draw into his concept of learning from this domain, then by his own words he includes under it everything that we learn from human beings, in contrast to what is invented from the mind; it is distinguished by him from philosophy as that which is a matter of fact (quod est facti) is distinguished from that which is a matter of pure knowledge or of right (quod est rationis sive iuris).
# generator = deepseek-flash + Stanza UD
# normalized_shadow = yes
