# sent_id = orat29.3.1
# text = Schon Demosthenes, indem er die Vortheile erwägt, welche ihm gegenüber der Selbstherrscher Philipp hatte, hebt trefflich hervor, dieser habe denen, welche ihm folgten, mit unbeschränkter Macht geboten, was im Kriege das erste von allem sei; dann hätten diese die Waffen stets in Händen gehabt; reich an Geld habe er gethan, was ihm jedesmal gefiel, ohne es in Volksbeschlüssen voraus zu verkünden, ohne von anderen zur Rechenschaft gezogen werden zu können, allein Herr, Anführer, Machthaber über alles.
# reading_translation = Even Demosthenes, when he weighs the advantages that the absolute ruler Philip had over him, excellently emphasizes that Philip commanded those who followed him with unlimited power in what is the first of all things in war; that these men then always had their weapons in their hands; that, rich in money, he did whatever pleased him each time, without announcing it beforehand in decrees of the people, without being able to be called to account by others—alone lord, leader, and potentate over all things.
